  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1215 AM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nOverall CONUS pattern during the next 7 days will be nearly dry over \nall of the region as mainly zonal flow will dominate, with the jet \nremaining to our north. One glancing blow will occur late Saturday, \nwith will cool temps down a few degrees but not much in the way of \nany precip is anticipated. The rest of the week max temps will \ngenerally be in the low 80s across the region with upper 60s over \nthe valleys.\n\nWith the flow aloft relatively weak, and with all of the precip that \noccurred over a good part of the region the last couple of days, no \nfire weather concerns are anticipated. \n\nLooking at the long term guidance, the next chance of any widespread \nprecip appears to occur after next weekend.",
